{"t": 1795077588.3812056, "tool": "analyze", "code": "import numpy as np\n# estimate local power-law exponent n(eps,T): regress log sigma on log eps within T bins\nfor lo,hi in [(2,2.5),(2.5,3),(3,3.5),(3.5,4),(4,4.5),(4.5,5),(5,5.5),(5.5,6)]:\n    m=(T>=lo)&(T<hi)\n    if m.sum()<4: continue\n    A=np.c_[np.ones(m.sum()),np.log(eps[m])]\n    c=np.linalg.lstsq(A,np.log(sigma[m]),rcond=None)[0]\n    r=np.log(sigma[m])-A@c\n    print(lo,hi,m.sum(),\"n=%.3f\"%c[1],\"A=%.3f\"%np.exp(c[0]),\"rms=%.4f\"%np.sqrt(np.mean(r**2)))\n", "out": "2 2.5 34 n=1.201 A=0.995 rms=0.1627\n2.5 3 27 n=1.037 A=1.328 rms=0.1490\n3 3.5 47 n=0.781 A=1.965 rms=0.2246\n3.5 4 39 n=0.751 A=2.357 rms=0.1623\n4 4.5 44 n=0.761 A=2.893 rms=0.1979\n4.5 5 39 n=0.618 A=4.053 rms=0.1715\n5 5.5 37 n=0.492 A=5.272 rms=0.2038\n5.5 6 33 n=0.461 A=6.838 rms=0.1936\n"}
